OPENRESTY-WEB-ARCHITECTURE(7)         System Administration         OPENRESTY-WEB-ARCHITECTURE(7)

NAME
       openresty-web-architecture - OpenResty and NodeJS web stack notes for this server

SYNOPSIS
       man openresty-web-architecture
       sudo openresty -t
       sudo systemctl reload openresty

OVERVIEW
       This  server  uses  OpenResty  as  the public HTTP/HTTPS edge and NodeJS services as local
       backends. Public web traffic is intended to enter through Cloudflare  edge  IPs  and  then
       reach OpenResty on ports 80 and 443. OpenResty terminates TLS, applies Lua-based controls,
       serves  static  assets,  and  reverse  proxies  selected  paths to local services bound to
       127.0.0.1.

MAIN COMPONENTS
       OpenResty
              Service:  openresty.service.   Main   config:   /usr/local/openresty/nginx/conf/ng‐
              inx.conf.  Site configs are included from /etc/openresty/conf.d/*.conf.

       Feathers host
              Service:   feathersjsapp.service.  Entry:  /opt/app/feathers/index.js.  Listens  on
              127.0.0.1:13010 and serves /app/notifier/api/, /app/realtimetext/api/, and /app/up‐
              dater/api/health through OpenResty.

       Admin auth service
              Service: lieyanbang-auth.service. Entry: /opt/lieyanbang-auth/src/server.js.   Lis‐
              tens on 127.0.0.1:3001 and handles /auth/ plus admin session introspection.

       ttyd WebSSH
              Service:  ttyd.service.  Listens on 127.0.0.1:7681 and is exposed below /tty/ after
              admin session validation.

OPENRESTY CONFIGURATION
       The active site file is /etc/openresty/conf.d/lieyanbang.conf. It  defines  upstreams  for
       lieyanbang_auth  and  lieyanbang_ttyd, redirects HTTP to HTTPS for lieyanbang.com, config‐
       ures certificates from /etc/letsencrypt/live/lieyanbang.com, and includes  additional  up‐
       dater app locations from /etc/openresty/conf.d/updater-apps/*.conf.

       The  global  nginx.conf  enables  gzip,  TLS  policy, Cloudflare-aware log fields, and Lua
       shared dictionaries named rate_limit_store and updater_token_cache. Lua files used by  the
       stack live in /usr/local/openresty/nginx/lua and /etc/openresty/lua.

REQUEST FLOW
       Static site
              / is served from /var/www/lieyanbang/html and returns 404 when a file is not found.

       Admin and ttyd
              /admin/,  /api/admin/,  and  /tty/  run /etc/openresty/lua/check_admin_session.lua.
              That script calls  the  internal  /__auth_introspect  location,  which  proxies  to
              lieyanbang_auth  /auth/introspect.  WebSocket  upgrade  traffic under /tty/ is kept
              open with long read/send timeouts and proxy buffering disabled.

       Application APIs
              /app/notifier/api/, /app/realtimetext/api/, and  /app/updater/api/health  proxy  to
              127.0.0.1:13010.  RealtimeText  also  forwards Cloudflare identity headers and sup‐
              ports WebSocket upgrade.

       Updater apps
              Updater endpoints are loaded from /etc/openresty/conf.d/updater-apps/*.conf and use
              Lua token helpers from /etc/openresty/lua where configured.

ROUTINE OPERATIONS
       Test configuration
              Run sudo openresty -t before reloads. A  successful  test  currently  reports  that
              /usr/local/openresty/nginx/conf/nginx.conf syntax is ok.

       Reload edge config
              Run sudo systemctl reload openresty after a passing config test.

       Inspect logs
              OpenResty  logs are under /usr/local/openresty/nginx/logs/. Service logs are avail‐
              able with journalctl -u openresty, journalctl -u feathersjsapp, and  journalctl  -u
              lieyanbang-auth.

       Add a new app path
              Prefer adding a location under /etc/openresty/conf.d/lieyanbang.conf or a small in‐
              cluded file when the app belongs to an include directory. Bind new Node services to
              127.0.0.1, add a systemd service, proxy only the needed paths, and run openresty -t
              before reload.

SECURITY NOTES
       UFW  is active with default deny incoming. Web ports 80 and 443 are allowed for Cloudflare
       IP ranges by /usr/local/bin/update-cloudflare-ips.sh, scheduled in root crontab  at  03:00
       daily.  Public  SSH on port 22 is denied, SSH on port 13027 is allowed, and tailnet SSH on
       tailscale0 port 22 is allowed.

       Fail2Ban is enabled with the sshd jail. Use sudo fail2ban-client status  sshd  to  inspect
       banned IPs and jail health.

FILES
       /etc/openresty/README.txt
              Short pointer for operators working in the OpenResty config directory.

       /etc/openresty/conf.d/lieyanbang.conf
              Primary site routing file.

       /usr/local/openresty/nginx/conf/nginx.conf
              OpenResty global config and include root.

SEE ALSO
       openresty(8), nginx(8), systemctl(1), journalctl(1), ufw(8), fail2ban-client(1), feathers-
       host(7)

