FEATHERS-HOST(7)                      System Administration                      FEATHERS-HOST(7)

NAME
       feathers-host - host layout for FeathersJS microservices under /opt/app/feathers

SYNOPSIS
       man feathers-host
       systemctl status feathersjsapp.service
       journalctl -u feathersjsapp.service -f

DESCRIPTION
       /opt/app/feathers is the host layer for FeathersJS-based microservices.  It keeps a shared
       host  entry  at  /opt/app/feathers/index.js, mounts service projects under this directory,
       and leaves room for additional microservices.

CURRENT LAYOUT
       /opt/app/feathers/index.js
              Host process entry started by feathersjsapp.service.

       /opt/app/feathers/realtimetext/
              Current FeathersJS app project.

       /opt/app/feathers/data/
              Runtime database files used by the host and application.

       /opt/app/feathers/logs/
              Runtime log files.

MOUNT RULE
       New service projects should be placed under /opt/app/feathers/<service-name>/ and  mounted
       by  the host layer instead of running as unrelated standalone paths.  The current app path
       is /opt/app/feathers/realtimetext/ and the current service entry is  /opt/app/feathers/in‐
       dex.js.

NOTES
       The external path /app/realtimetext/* is still kept as-is. The current host code registers
       realtimetext  through  registerRealtimeText(...) on the shared host app.  If more services
       are added later, extend /opt/app/feathers/index.js.

FILES
       /etc/systemd/system/feathersjsapp.service
              Production systemd service for the host.

       /opt/app/feathers/README.txt
              Pointer file replacing the former README.md.

SEE ALSO
       systemctl(1), journalctl(1), openresty-web-architecture(7)

